WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.543 --> 00:00:04.054
- [Man] Do you think that
Alvin's gonna be able to do it?

00:00:04.054 --> 00:00:07.140
- If anyone's gonna do
it, it's gonna be Alvin.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.203
- There's no way, it's impossible.

00:00:09.203 --> 00:00:10.723
- If anyone can do it, Alvin can do it.

00:00:10.723 --> 00:00:12.510
- Alvin can do anything.

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:13.343
- [Alvin] I feel like my whole

00:00:13.343 --> 00:00:14.840
life has lead up to this point.

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:20.990
Today, we're making the 100 layer lasagna,

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:22.700
it's gonna be great, I'm a little nervous,

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.960
100 layers is a lot of layers,
I've never made this before.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.963
It's kind of a crazy idea,
and hopefully it goes well.

00:00:30.243 --> 00:00:33.137
Oh, I forgot my concealer,
hold on, I need to.

00:00:33.137 --> 00:00:35.040
No, I need to put on concealer, hold on.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.070
The ladies at Sephora
were very patient with

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.170
me when I learned how to do this.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:41.490
Not gonna get on the food, I promise.

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:43.053
But, you know, gotta take care of

00:00:43.053 --> 00:00:46.400
these hands because I throw them a lot.

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:48.860
The idea for the 100
layered lasagna kind of

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:51.050
came from an internet challenge.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.900
It was kind of like this
100 layers of makeup,

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.316
100 layers of clothes,
and we work at Tasty,

00:00:55.316 --> 00:00:57.570
so like why not do 100 layers of food,

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:01.180
and lasagna was the first
layered food that came to mind.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:03.369
So instead of doing the
usual ricotta mixture

00:01:03.369 --> 00:01:06.230
and a chunky meat sauce,
I went for a thinner

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:08.548
meat sauce and a bechamel
because when I assemble

00:01:08.548 --> 00:01:10.119
the lasagna, this is going to help

00:01:10.119 --> 00:01:12.773
keep those layers nice and smooth.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:16.900
When I'm done, this will
have 50 layers of noodles,

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:20.743
and 50 layers of sauce for
a grand total of 100 layers.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:24.410
The biggest hurdle with
this is going to be its

00:01:24.410 --> 00:01:27.677
size and how it is
contained, because there's no

00:01:27.677 --> 00:01:32.010
baking dish that can fit a 100
layer lasagna, and you know,

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:33.810
you could definitely go and maybe get a

00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:37.110
custom metal pan, but to
do this at home I wanted to

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.450
see how you could maybe customize or

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:42.400
MacGyver regular baking
dishes to fit this.

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:44.500
It's gonna be really tall, and definitely

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:47.180
figuring out how to bake
it while maintaining

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:49.220
its height and size was
the most difficult part.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.739
I thought of using foils
and lasagna noodles to

00:01:51.739 --> 00:01:55.260
sort of hold the foil up, and
to make these four walls to

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:58.360
contain the lasagna while it
baked, and I hope it works.

00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:00.700
So I'll start with the
pan as a base, and as the

00:02:00.700 --> 00:02:02.990
lasagna gets taller and taller
and taller, we're gonna put

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.510
the walls in to help keep it in place.

00:02:05.510 --> 00:02:09.960
Each layer needs to be extremely
level and extremely smooth.

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.960
Guys, I think I lost track, I'm at like 5.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:13.750
Does anybody have a
piece of paper and a pen?

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:15.783
It's almost like Jenga,
if you do it all one way,

00:02:15.783 --> 00:02:17.779
the lasagna might split
down the middle, but if

00:02:17.779 --> 00:02:20.270
you can alternate them it'll
create this interlocking

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:23.120
pattern that'll help them stay
more stable when you cut it.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:24.680
I just put the foil walls on because

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:26.943
I want to make sure it doesn't collapse.

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:32.740
But I would feel bad about
naming my lasagna because then I

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:36.628
would cut it open and it would
be eaten by like 500 people.

00:02:36.628 --> 00:02:41.052
I think George would be
nice, but spelled Sjors.

00:02:41.052 --> 00:02:44.090
41, ladies and gentlemen, 41.

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:47.962
I would make this for a
really big party if I'm really

00:02:47.962 --> 00:02:52.290
trying to show off to a bunch
of fancy people, I don't know.

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:53.920
I also just might make it for lunch.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:55.520
Don't get lost in the sauce, kids.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:02:57.540
I think we're in a good
spot, not gonna lie,

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.270
it's still not over the
edge and we've only got

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:03.010
seven more, so I'm feeling
pretty good about this.

00:03:03.010 --> 00:03:05.634
You know, it could just
totally collapse and

00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:08.633
explode, and you know,
then it's not all good.

00:03:09.591 --> 00:03:12.758
(upbeat, jazzy music)

